(a) It shall be unlawful to use a purchasing card to make any purchase unauthorized by this section or otherwise unrelated to official Macon-Bibb County business. Any person who violates this subsection shall be personally liable to Macon-Bibb County for the amount of the purchase and prosecuted to the fullest extent of the law. The foregoing penalties are in addition to the penalties described in subsection (i) of this section.
(b) A purchasing card shall not be used for:
(1) Goods or services for personal use;
(2) Alcoholic beverages;
(3) Tobacco products;
(4) Meals, except meals for Macon-Bibb County officials and employees during authorized business or travel for which no per diem is provided and meals for the mayor and the mayor's guests and/or the county manager and his or her guests, while conducting official Macon-Bibb County business, or meals for team building or morale purposes may be authorized subject to preapproval by the county manager;
(5) Cash advances;
(6) Gift cards, stored value cards, calling cards pre-paid cards, or similar items.
(c) A purchasing card may be used only for:
(1) Services and supplies not to exceed two thousand five hundred dollars ($2,500.00). Purchases shall not be artificially divided so as to circumvent the two thousand five hundred dollar ($2,500.00) limit;
(2) Authorized travel expenses of elected officials, the county manager, Macon-Bibb County attorney, clerk of commission, municipal court clerk, department heads or their designee while on official Macon-Bibb County business.
(3) Purchases over two thousand five hundred dollars ($2,500.00) which are expressly authorized as a small or routine purchase under Section 19-5.3 of this Chapter.
(4) Purchasing cards shall be used to make any eligible purchases wherever feasible. No authorized user of a purchasing card shall make by requisition any purchase authorized and reasonably able to be made by purchasing card.
(d) The Macon-Bibb County procurement director may provide purchasing cards to select offices and departments (hereinafter "agencies") of Macon-Bibb County. Each purchasing card is issued in the name of the department head or designee who shall:
(1) Ensure that the use of each card is accounted for on forms provided by the procurement department;
(2) Ensure that each card is secured when not in use;
(3) Designate which subordinates, if any, are authorized to use a purchasing card;
(4) Ensure that the monthly billing for each card is reconciled and submitted with corresponding receipts to Macon-Bibb County procurement department in a timely manner;
(5) Ensure that any billing discrepancies are resolved with the vendor;
(6) Document any unauthorized use of a purchasing card and report same to the administration;
(7) Document any vendor disputes related to purchasing card and report same to the Purchasing Card Administrator on at least a quarterly basis; and
(8) Notify the Purchasing Card Administrator immediately upon learning that a card is lost or stolen.
(e) When a department receives a monthly billing statement for purchases made on a purchasing card, the department head or his designee shall:
(1) Verify the accuracy of the monthly billing statement by comparing each purchase with the corresponding receipt;
(2) Complete and sign a submission statement on forms provided by the procurement department; and
(3) Submit the reconciled monthly billing statement, corresponding receipts, and submission statement to the Purchasing Card Coordinator(s) within ten (10) business days of the date the monthly billing statement was received by the agency.
(f) No person shall use a purchasing card without first signing for the card on a log sheet provided by the procurement department.
(g) As soon as reasonably possible after using a purchasing card, the purchaser shall complete and sign the log sheet provided by the procurement department and return the card with all receipts to the department head or his designee. Repeated or unjustified failure to provide receipts may result in the purchaser being held personally liable to Macon-Bibb County for the amount of the purchase in addition to any other penalties authorized by this section.
(h) Any purchaser who fails to produce a required receipt shall provide a written explanation to the department head or his designee for submission to the procurement department. The explanation shall include, at a minimum, a description of the items purchased, the name of the vendor, the reason for the purchaser's failure to produce the receipt, and the efforts the purchaser made to produce the receipt. Failure to provide an adequate explanation may result in the purchaser being held personally liable to Macon-Bibb County for the amount of the purchase in addition to any other penalties authorized by this section.
(i) Failure to comply with the provisions of this section shall be grounds for disciplinary action up to and including discharge and the loss of purchasing card privileges. In the case of an elected official, upon resolution of the governing authority, failure to comply with the provisions of this section shall be grounds for public censure and the loss of purchasing card privileges.
(Ord. No. O-15-0060, § 1, 12-15-2015; Ord. No. O-18-0089, § 1, 10-2-2018; Ord. No. O-21-0084, § 1, 10-19-2021)

